  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2ee87e681215b6147a44021cf30db039, type: 3}
  m_Name: 1.Biblioteca
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  nameOfPoint: Biblioteca
  coordinatesPoint: {x: 14.51364, y: 35.89837}
  firstPartInfo: "I start my journey at the hub of all things research: the National
    Library. Rows of shelves from floor to ceiling full of precariously preserved
    leather-bound volumes. A treasure and a labyrinth all at once. Amidst my perusal
    of the Government Gazette microfilms, an <link=Image_1><u><color=blue>avviso</link></u></color>
    (notice) catches my eye. It\u2019s written in Italian, the official language
    of the island back in the early 1800s. It refers to the execution of one Antonio
    Borg on the 17th of August 1813 as a penalty for his breaking quarantine rules.
    Obviously the recent Covid-19 pandemic was not the first to visit Malta. On a
    small island like Malta, an outbreak should be taken seriously since contamination
    is imminent. Many people were fined during 2020-2021, but to kill a person for
    not observing the government\u2019s restrictions takes it too far. I am intrigued
    by the singularity of the case and decide to investigate further."
  secondPartInfo: The avviso does not specify where Borg was captured or the details
    of his arrest and execution. From another source, I find out that he was caught
    conducting a cart from which bread was being distributed in Merchant Street near
    the fountain "<link=Image_2><u><color=blue>altrevolte detta de Orefice.</link></u></color>".
    Thus it was decreed and pronounced and Borg was executed on the following day,
    the 17th of August, in Merchant Street at the same place where he had been caught
    and arrested for breaking the regulations. This Orefice still stands at the corner
    with the street that houses all the famous filigree shops of Valletta.
  imgMarker: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c98feaebd40d8df449e6d3855ac84352, type: 3}
  imgMain: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f26fa8880b3aeef4b8516c82dc12f2a5, type: 3}
  nameOfStory: Quarantine
  hintOfPOI: "Orefice you say? It means jeweller. There is a street perpendicular
    to Merchant Street that is full of those. It\u2019s a street that\u2019s bright
    like gold - and this brightness is reflected in its name!"
  solutionOfPOI: The street is Santa Lucia. So the location you are looking for should
    be at the corner of Merchant and Santa Lucia Street.
